{
  "comment": "The label font stack, in order -- ADR-100. Read by tools/make-glyphs.py, which draws the tile face's glyph ranges from it, and embedded in Graticula.Render.Skia, which draws the raster face's labels from it, so the two faces cannot disagree about which font a codepoint comes from. A codepoint is drawn by the first font that claims its block and has it, else by the first font that has it. An optional font is not checked in: make-glyphs.py --cjk fetches it from url at build time and refuses it unless its SHA-256 matches, and the renderer uses it only when it sits in the fonts directory beside the server.",
